","T1105"],"references":["https:\/\/blog.talosintelligence.com\/the-n8n-n8mare\/"],"industries":["NGO","Education"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"69dfb91808e1258915184d6e","name":"From fake Proton VPN sites to gaming mods, this Windows infostealer is everywhere","description":"Multiple campaigns are distributing NWHStealer through diverse platforms including fake VPN downloads, hardware utilities, and gaming modifications. The infostealer collects browser data, saved passwords, and cryptocurrency wallet information. Distribution occurs via fake websites impersonating legitimate services like Proton VPN, code hosting platforms such as GitHub and GitLab, file hosting services including MediaFire and SourceForge, and links from YouTube videos. Two primary infection methods are analyzed: one using a free web hosting provider distributing malicious ZIP files with self-injection loaders, and another employing fake websites with DLL hijacking techniques that inject into the RegAsm process. The stealer targets over 25 cryptocurrency wallets and multiple browsers, exfiltrating data to command-and-control servers using AES-CBC encryption and maintaining persistence through scheduled tasks and UAC bypass techniques.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-04-15T17:21:00.985000","created":"2026-04-15T16:13:12.178000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4175716022,"indicator":"get-proton-vpn.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-04-15T16:13:13","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4226921748,"indicator":"vpn-proton-setup.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-04-15T16:13:13","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4305886746,"indicator":"newworld-helloworld.icu","type":"domain","created":"2026-04-15T16:13:13","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4312159633,"indicator":"5cb3b902ae5993ae4e502f1c29cfb4e0","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-04-15T16:13:13","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4312159634,"indicator":"8ef6bcde887786d1a96497fa9aa04fd4e1eb02b0","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-04-15T16:13:13","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4312159635,"indicator":"2494709b8a2646640b08b1d5d75b6bfb3167540ed4acdb55ded050f6df9c53b3","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-04-15T16:13:13","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4312159636,"indicator":"e97cb6cbcf2583fe4d8dcabd70d3f67f6cc977fc9a8cbb42f8a2284efe24a1e3","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-04-15T16:13:13","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4312159637,"indicator":"https:\/\/www.onworks.net\/software\/windows\/app-hardware-visualizer","type":"URL","created":"2026-04-15T16:13:13","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["cryptocurrency theft","browser data theft","fake websites","infostealer","nwhstealer"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["NWHStealer"],"attack_ids":["T1539","T1548.002","T1082","T1140","T1567","T1036","T1055","T1218.003","T1555.003","T1083","T1204","T1059.001","T1547.001","T1566","T1562.001","T1055.012","T1027","T1573","T1132","T1105"],"references":["https:\/\/securityboulevard.com\/2026\/04\/from-fake-proton-vpn-sites-to-gaming-mods-this-windows-infostealer-is-everywhere\/"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"69dfc7dfb590f3df513f5fee","name":"Silent Crypto Wallet Takeover Unlimited USDT Approval Exploitation via Trust Wallet QR Code Phishing","description":"An active campaign targets Trust Wallet users through malicious QR codes distributed via Telegram, exploiting deep link mechanisms to redirect victims to Netlify-hosted phishing domains. The attack masquerades as a legitimate USDT transfer interface but covertly triggers an ERC-20 approve() transaction, granting unlimited token allowance to an attacker-controlled contract on BNB Smart Chain. This enables persistent fund drainage without further victim interaction. The modular drainer architecture uses config.js for control parameters and main.js for execution logic, with integrated Telegram bot infrastructure providing real-time transaction monitoring. Analysis confirms 52 transaction notifications indicating active exploitation. The campaign employs social engineering through a deceptive dollar-one illusion where victims believe they are initiating small transactions while actually granting unlimited wallet access. Multiple cloned phishing domains demonstrate scalable deployment within a Drainer-as-a-Servic","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-04-15T17:20:30.813000","created":"2026-04-15T17:16:15.355000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4312725431,"indicator":"6f25ebdc95eb23935abefc67150e05fe471d2d02","type":"YARA","created":"2026-04-15T17:16:16","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4312783453,"indicator":"https:\/\/link.trustwallet.com\/open_url?coin_id=60&url=https:\/\/swift-wallat-usdt-send.netlify.app","type":"URL","created":"2026-04-15T17:19:58","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4312783454,"indicator":"https:\/\/send-usdt-09-admin.netlify.app","type":"URL","created":"2026-04-15T17:19:58","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4312783455,"indicator":"https:\/\/swift-wallat-usdt-send.netlify.app","type":"URL","created":"2026-04-15T17:19:58","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["crypto drainer","qr code phishing","token approval abuse","trust wallet","drainer-as-a-service","usdt","telegram bot","deep link exploitation","bnb smart chain"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":["T1583","T1539","T1204.002","T1566.002","T1071","T1608.001","T1185","T1102","T1608","T1583.006","T1528","T1204","T1098","T1048","T1566","T1573","T1056","T1134","T1071.001","T1102.001","T1048.003"],"references":["https:\/\/www.cyfirma.com\/research\/silent-crypto-wallet-takeover-unlimited-usdt-approval-exploitation-via-trust-wallet-qr-code-phishing"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"69dfc7cd3be10faa299f8741","name":"Fake YouTube copyright notices can steal your Google login","description":"A sophisticated phishing campaign is targeting YouTube creators using convincing fake copyright strike notifications. The attack dynamically pulls real channel data including profile pictures, subscriber counts, and recent videos to create personalized scare pages. Victims are funneled through a Browser-in-the-Browser attack displaying a fake Google sign-in that captures credentials. The operation functions as phishing-as-a-service, with multiple attackers sharing infrastructure and rotating domains to evade detection. Successful attacks result in complete Google account takeover, allowing hijackers to rebrand channels and livestream cryptocurrency scams to existing audiences. The kit automatically exempts channels with over three million subscribers to avoid detection by security teams.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-04-15T17:16:45.864000","created":"2026-04-15T17:15:57.258000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4312721418,"indicator":"blacklivesmattergood4.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-04-15T17:15:58","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4312721419,"indicator":"dmca-notification.info","type":"domain","created":"2026-04-15T17:15:58","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4312721420,"indicator":"dopozj.net","type":"domain","created":"2026-04-15T17:15:58","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4312721421,"indicator":"ec40pr.net","type":"domain","created":"2026-04-15T17:15:58","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4312721422,"indicator":"xddlov.net","type":"domain","created":"2026-04-15T17:15:58","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["browser-in-the-browser","google account takeover","phishing campaign","credential theft","cryptocurrency scams"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":[],"references":["https:\/\/securityboulevard.com\/2026\/04\/fake-youtube-copyright-notices-can-steal-your-google-login\/"],"industries":["Media","Technology"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"69dfa90cbce3255033d01a33","name":"New ransomware targets Turkey via Adwind RAT","description":"A threat cluster has been identified leveraging a customized Adwind (Java RAT) variant with polymorphic characteristics to deliver JanaWare ransomware. The campaign specifically targets Turkish users through geofencing mechanisms that check system locale and external IP geolocation. Active since at least 2020, the operation primarily affects home users and small to medium-sized businesses. Initial access occurs via phishing emails with malicious Java archives distributed through Google Drive links. The ransomware employs AES encryption and communicates over Tor networks, demanding modest ransoms between $200-$400. The malware uses multiple obfuscation techniques including Stringer and Allatori obfuscators, implements file pumping for polymorphism, and disables Windows security features before encryption. Victims are instructed to contact attackers through qTox or dedicated Tor onion sites.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-04-15T16:01:15.96200